# Allure — all generated.
#
# allure-history.json is ignored too, though it is the one file that carries
# the trend. Committing it would mean shipping a quarter-megabyte of run data
# from whichever laptop generated it last, which is noise to a reader and
# merge conflicts to a contributor. A real deployment keeps history in CI
# (cached, or written back by the reporting job) rather than in the repo.
# The json reporter, written only in CI for the on-demand callback.
results.json

allure-results/
allure-report/
allure-history.json
